# Where the keyboard goes: back to the list when the address box is put away, to whichever view is
# showing when the view mode changes, and the context-menu key (Apps, Shift+F10) opening the menu a
# right-click would.

tree .
refresh
focus FileListView
assert-focus FileListView

# The address box takes the keys while it is up, and gives them back to the list when Esc puts it away.
window-key Ctrl+L
assert-focus PathBox
window-key Esc
assert-focus FileListView

# Thumbnails on: the tiles take the focus the hidden list had, and give it back.
thumbnails 0.5
assert-focus FileTileView
thumbnails 0
assert-focus FileListView

# The context-menu key opens the selection's menu, as a right-click on it would.
select notes.txt
window-key Shift+F10
assert-menu-open
shot 01-context-key
window-key Esc
assert-menu-closed
window-key Apps
assert-menu-open
window-key Esc
assert-menu-closed

# The tree's menu from the keyboard.
focus FolderTree
window-key Shift+F10
assert-menu-open
shot 02-tree-context-key
window-key Esc

# Ctrl+arrow moves the cursor and leaves the selection; Space then selects the row it is on.
focus FileListView
select notes.txt
window-key Ctrl+Down
window-key Space
assert-selected 1

# The breadcrumb is a Tab stop, as the original's crumbs were buttons: Left picks the crumb above the
# folder you are in, Enter goes there. A click on a crumb leaves the keyboard with the list.
go Documents
focus Breadcrumb
assert-focus Breadcrumb
window-key Left
shot 03-breadcrumb-key
window-key Enter
assert-row Documents
